subproblems.statement:
For all natural numbers P and n there is a continuous linear map L from n-vectors Λₙ(ℝ^P) (MultiVector P n, the continuous linear functionals on n-covectors) to n-covectors Λⁿ(ℝ^P) (Covector (Euclid P) n) with the following property. For every ξ ∈ Λₙ and every linear subspace Q ⊆ ℝ^P with IsUnitOrientationOf ξ Q, i.e. there are an orthonormal family τ = (τ_0, …, τ_{n−1}) spanning Q and a sign s ∈ {1, −1} with ξ(α) = s·α(τ) for every n-covector α:
(a) |ξ(α)| ≤ |α| for every n-covector α, where |α| = covectorEuclideanNorm α = (Σ_{I : Fin n → Fin P strictly increasing} α(e_{I(0)}, …, e_{I(n−1)})²)^{1/2};
(b) |L(ξ)| ≤ 1;
(c) ξ(L(ξ)) = 1.
